-- title:
--   Common level-stable affine chart for the ends of the blow-up
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which (`hH₁`) is the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which (`hK`) equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian local discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$ (`hζA`), and let $K$ carry an $A$-algebra structure compatible with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C$ for `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $X$ for [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and the corresponding chart for $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $\jmath$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\jmath$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the Drinfeld-chart datum at all supersingular points over $\varpi$; its conclusion is a conjunction of seven clauses, summarised here) requires: for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global image of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ whose residue $j$-invariant is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a discrete valuation domain $W$ complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v - fu\bigr)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the germ map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ through the chart: (i) $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the constant $\sigma a$; (ii) every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$ — this predicate says that $\tau$ realises, on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, the weight-$k$ slash action of `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` (the matrix of $\gamma^{-1}$ with off-diagonal entries scaled by $q$), read through any $\iota$ as above; (iii) for such $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$ the induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for every such $\gamma, \tau$ whose induced endomorphism of $C$ is trivial modulo $y'$ there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta \circ e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} = e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} \circ \tau$, with $\theta$ fixing the constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) two primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both images of $X_0$ and $X_1$, each containing the constant $\sigma\varpi$, and containing elements $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ and $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (v) containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, the germ of $a \in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $j$-expansion with exponents multiplied by $q$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of these two elements in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a, b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the value $\sum_{i \le e_0} \operatorname{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and the image under $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of that difference equals the class of $h$.
--
--   Fixed next are a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`) whose residue $j$-invariant is supersingular (`hss'`), with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`), together with an explicit chart datum at $z$: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, power series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with $S_1 = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for this datum, exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   The remaining data are: an ideal $J$ of $C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum of the family of ideals obtained, for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ mapping $C$ into $C$, by contracting the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the images of the constant $\sigma_1\varpi_t$ and of $X_0, X_1$ along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ and then pulling back along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$; an $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$; and a valuation subring $W$ of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` has two clauses: $C \subseteq B$, and every $f \in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$. The hypothesis `hR2` has three clauses: $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` has five clauses: an element of $L$ lies in $W$ if and only if it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ if and only if it lies in $W$ and in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $f \in W$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. The hypothesis `hEQ` has five clauses: first, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose vanishing locus is exactly the set of $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant in the sense that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) such that $\rho(\tau b) =$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c)$ applied to $\rho(b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau b \in B$, and $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; second, level automorphisms at elements of $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; third, for every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ has $\tau b \in B$ with $\tau b \in Q$; fourth, if $b \in B$ satisfies $\tau b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all such $\gamma, \tau$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$; fifth, a level automorphism at an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ (in the sense that $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y$ for $b \in C$ with $\tau b \in C$) preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally, `ends` is a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ belongs to it if and only if there is $a \in J$, non-zero in $K$, such that, with $B_a$ the $A$-subalgebra generated over $C$ by all $x \in K$ with $xa \in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ for which $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (that is, $f \in O$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$), every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $O$ does not contain $B$. The hypothesis `hperm` states that every level automorphism at an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $W$ permutes `ends`, in the sense that for each $O \in$ `ends` there is $O' \in$ `ends` with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$. Lastly, $n$ is a natural number and $\mathsf{S} \in C$ an element with (`hS`) $n \ge 1$, $\mathsf{S} \in J^n$, $\mathsf{S} \ne 0$ in $K$, $\mathsf{S}$ fixed by every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, and $i\mathsf{S}^{-1} \in O$ for every $O \in$ `ends` and every $i \in J^n$.
--
--   Under all these hypotheses there exists an $A$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K$ such that: $A \to B_c$ is of finite type; $B_c$ is stable under every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and for every $O \in$ `ends`, first $B_c \subseteq O$, and second $O$ is the localisation of $B_c$ at the units of $O$, in the sense that $f \in O$ if and only if there are $g, h \in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ (whenever $h$ lies in $O$) and $fh = g$.
--
--   This is the construction, for the auxiliary full level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with its $\ell$-diamond condition, of a single finitely generated and level-equivariant affine chart of the blow-up of the supersingular chart of the integral model that simultaneously dominates and localises to all of its ends. It is used in the assembly [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), where the auxiliary data (invariant section, blow-up chart, Drinfeld chart witnesses) are produced rather than assumed.
